    },
    {
      "Seq": 11,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I turn to the wolf, its form as stark and unforgiving as the day my grandfather warned us of dangers hidden in the shadows. The growl from its chest echoes a memory of looters, their cold eyes and ruthless hands. This one means me harm, just as they did, and I must stay wary and ready.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 12,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I perceive a wolf, its fur rangy, fangs bared, a deep growl rumbling from its chest. I want to examine this creature closely, for it marks the edge of our survival here. I will use the practical skill of staying alive in these harsh conditions, where waiting has a price.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 13,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I step closer, not to watch, but to taste what I can find. Hot sun beats, I need something now.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 14,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I will not examine the wolf closely, for waiting past its hour only dulls my senses to the wildness that comes before it. I could still examine the wolf closely, another way now. The carcass\u0027s joints will speak their readiness, their swell and colour, their scent turning just before the meat goes bad.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 15,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I cannot peer closely, for the wolf stands here, a threat real and raw. The blade is sharp, but my sight is clouded by the beast\u0027s looming presence.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 16,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I notice the wolf\u0027s rangy form, its fur a stark contrast to the parched earth, and the scent of salt and fear rises with the heat. The growl rolls through the air, a warning that is also a testament to its strength. I want to slay it, but the practical skill of staying alive in this harsh steppe guides me. I will rely on my knowledge of this place, the calm that comes from knowing the hour a thing is at its best, to avoid the folly of impatience and wait until the time is right.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 17,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I shun it, fearing what it might breed.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 18,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Hot steppe",
      "Area": "Clearing",
      "LocationId": 7471,
      "Actor": "Haralhd",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I see the beast\u0027s weight swell, its skin a deep colour of ripe flesh, and the scent of it comes up, just before it turns. So, I will not rush it, for waiting past its hour is a cruel price to pay. I could yet slay it, another way. I will rely on the plain ways of country folk, their calm in the heat, their senses sharp as a blade\u0027s edge, their readiness as clear as the scent of the dying blooms.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    }
